.TH SHCOMP 1
.SH NAME
shcomp \- Manage shell completions that follow the active tool version
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshcomp\fR [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage shell completions that follow the active tool version
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Print more detail; repeat for more
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
Report errors only
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinstall\fR
Install and reconcile shell shims for the selected tools
.TP
\fBuninstall\fR
Remove shcomp\-owned shims
.TP
\fBcomplete\-word\fR
Probe completion candidates through the target shell
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check the configuration and installed shims
.TP
\fBls\fR
List selected tools and their completion sources
.TP
\fBsearch\fR
Search the registry for a tool to add
.TP
\fBwhich\fR
Explain how one command is completed, without running it
.TP
\fBadd\fR
Add tool selections to the config, or describe a new command
.TP
\fBedit\fR
Edit the config in $VISUAL or $EDITOR, validated before it is written
.TP
\fBclean\fR
Remove cached completion scripts, or only the stale ones
.TP
\fBschema\fR
Print the JSON Schema for the config or a registry item
.TP
\fBusage\fR
Print the usage KDL for shcomp itself
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR
Print a completion script for shcomp itself
.SH "SHCOMP INSTALL"
Install and reconcile shell shims for the selected tools
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp install [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-fetch\fR
Do not fetch URL sources
.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
Fail instead of fetching an uncached URL source
.TP
\fB\-\-prewarm\fR
Generate scripts for the versions on PATH even when `[settings].prewarm` is false
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-prewarm\fR
Do not generate scripts now; the first Tab generates them
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would change without changing it
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Shells to reconcile; defaults to the `shells` setting
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP UNINSTALL"
Remove shcomp\-owned shims
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp uninstall [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would be removed without removing it
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Shells to clean; defaults to the `shells` setting
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP COMPLETE-WORD"
Probe completion candidates through the target shell
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp complete\-word [OPTIONS] <TOOL> [<WORDS>] ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Target shell; defaults to `$SHELL` when that is zsh or fish, otherwise zsh
.TP
\fB\-\-cword\fR \fI<CWORD>\fR
Index of the word being completed; defaults to the last word
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<TOOL>\fR
Tool reference, optionally with `@version`
.TP
\fB<WORDS>\fR
Words typed so far, starting with the command
.SH "SHCOMP DOCTOR"
Check the configuration and installed shims
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp doctor [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Run each generator and validate its output
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP LS"
List selected tools and their completion sources
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp ls [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Include disabled selections
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
Do not print the table header
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Describe one shell: its source and cache state, and only tools that complete in it
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP SEARCH"
Search the registry for a tool to add
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp search [OPTIONS] [<NAME>]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-i, \-\-interactive\fR
Pick a result from a menu and add it to the config
.TP
\fB\-m, \-\-match\-type\fR \fI<MATCH_TYPE>\fR
Match type: equal, contains, or fuzzy
.RS
\fIDefault: \fRfuzzy
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-header\fR
Do not print the table header
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-\-complete\fR
Print every candidate with its description, for shell completions
.TP
\fB\-\-complete\-ids\fR
Print only candidate values, for shell completions
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<NAME>\fR
Name, workspace, or reference to search for
.SH "SHCOMP WHICH"
Explain how one command is completed, without running it
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp which [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Only this shell; defaults to every installed shell
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<COMMAND>\fR
The command as you type it; an alias works too
.SH "SHCOMP ADD"
Add tool selections to the config, or describe a new command
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp add [OPTIONS] [<REFERENCE>] ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-alias\fR \fI<ALIAS>\fR
Extra command name to register; repeat for several
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR \fI<RUN>\fR
Command printing the completion, for every shell; `{shell}` and `{bin}` are filled in
.TP
\fB\-\-run\-zsh\fR \fI<RUN_ZSH>\fR
Command printing the zsh completion
.TP
\fB\-\-run\-fish\fR \fI<RUN_FISH>\fR
Command printing the fish completion
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Completion file to fetch, for the one `\-\-shell`
.TP
\fB\-\-usage\fR \fI<USAGE>\fR
Command printing a usage KDL spec, rendered by the `usage` CLI
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Shells the described command completes in; defaults to the installed ones
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
Description for the described command
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would change without changing anything
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\-code\fR
With \-\-dry\-run, exit 1 when there is something to do
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\fR
Write the selection but install nothing
.TP
\fB\-f, \-\-force\fR
Replace the selection's aliases instead of adding to them
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-prewarm\fR
Do not generate the script now; the first Tab generates it
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<REFERENCE>\fR
Tool references to add; with a source flag, the one command to describe
.SH "SHCOMP EDIT"
Edit the config in $VISUAL or $EDITOR, validated before it is written
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp edit [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-install\fR
Write the config but install nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-prewarm\fR
Do not generate scripts now; the first Tab generates them
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP CLEAN"
Remove cached completion scripts, or only the stale ones
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp clean [OPTIONS] [<TOOL>] ...
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-stale\fR
Remove only scripts no `shcomp load` can reach any more
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-shell\fR \fI<SHELL>\fR
Only this shell's scripts
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-dry\-run\fR
Print what would be removed without removing it
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<TOOL>\fR
Only these tools' scripts; defaults to every tool
.SH "SHCOMP SCHEMA"
Print the JSON Schema for the config or a registry item
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp schema [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-\-registry\fR
Print the registry\-item schema instead of the config schema
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP USAGE"
Print the usage KDL for shcomp itself
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp usage [OPTIONS]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH "SHCOMP COMPLETION"
Print a completion script for shcomp itself
.PP
\fBUsage:\fR shcomp completion [OPTIONS] <SHELL>
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
Print help
\fBArguments:\fR
.PP
.TP
\fB<SHELL>\fR
Shell to generate completions for
